id: pm-m6ig79
title: "Pull-request CI requests 33 hosted-runner jobs per push against the account's 20-job concurrency cap, so required checks wait hours before they start"
description: "Every push to a pm-cli pull request starts 25 CI jobs plus 8 jobs in CodeQL, Docs, Security and CodSpeed: 33 jobs against a GitHub Free account cap of 20 concurrent jobs (5 macOS) shared by about 30 ecosystem repositories. pm-cli alone therefore always queues, and under ecosystem load required checks start hours late. Ten of the 25 CI jobs are sub-minute runtime probes (Runtime smoke x3, Packed first run x6, Telemetry regression) that each pay a full queue wait and runner setup. The Windows cohorts also ran with max-parallel 2, which queued the 10-minute native cohort behind a script shard, so even an idle account took 28 minutes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,github-actions,performance,runner-queue
created_at: "2026-10-30T15:20:03.397Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T01:49:00.322Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T23:45:27.683Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-30T23:45:27.683Z"
claim_principal: "harness:claude-code#7b0e58428f53e3aaeaafb372"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "build-test runs one job per OS that performs the Node 22.18.0 and Node 24 packed first runs, the dist version smoke, the Node 22 telemetry and snapshot regressions (ubuntu), the native macOS checks and the full Windows npx/bunx acceptance; first-run and node22-telemetry jobs are gone; gates matrix is static+smokes: typecheck runs in static, both compatibility gates run in smokes, and the duplicated contracts:check/sdk:surface:check invocations are removed (quality:static still runs both checks); windows-regression-cohorts has no max-parallel cap; ci-workflow-contract, packed-first-run, node22-telemetry-workflow tests, gate-registry.json and defect-recurrence-policy.json reference the new job layout and pass; gate-registry passes; main branch protection requires Packed runtime (ubuntu-latest|macos-latest|windows-latest) instead of the ten removed names, and no required check is left that no workflow emits; the PR introducing the change records its uncontended wall clock and per-job durations"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "GitHub-hosted runners, GitHub Free personal account unbraind (20 concurrent jobs, 5 macOS), 2026-10-30"
resolution: "#1634 (merge 20e91f2f9) folds the packed first runs, version smoke, Node 22 telemetry/snapshot regressions, native macOS checks and Windows npx/bunx acceptance into one Packed runtime job per OS, moves typecheck into static and both compatibility gates into smokes, drops duplicated contract/surface checks and the Windows cohort cap; main's required checks were updated from 26 to 17 contexts."
expected_result: "A pm-cli PR push requests at most 15 CI jobs (23 across all PR workflows) while every proof that ran before still runs, the Windows cohorts run concurrently, and the uncontended CI wall clock stays under 20 minutes."
actual_result: "PR #1634 head ba4e7a853, CI run 41136001358: 15 CI jobs ran (23 across CI, CodSpeed, CodeQL, Docs and the 5 security jobs), all green. Longest jobs: Gates (static) 13.1 min, Packed runtime (windows-latest) 12.8 min, Windows native cohort 7.6 min, slowest coverage shard 7.2 min; the three Windows cohorts ran concurrently. Uncontended critical path is about 15 min (build 1.6 min + static 13.1 min). Contended wall clock was 36 min because coverage and Linux jobs queued behind other repositories for up to 25 minutes on the shared 20-job account cap (owner pm-gzr4j6)."
component: ci
